tellraw @a {"text": "remaining thrust over the aisle roofs to outer piers, so walls can be mostly glass.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Masons set out the geometry with compasses and templates (no structural theory); each", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "element was proportioned by rule of thumb and by what had stood. Beauvais' choir (48 m)", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "collapsed in 1284 at the limit. Stained glass was coloured in the melt with metal oxides", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "and held in lead cames.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "See it in context: /function ac:paris/notre_dame", "color": "aqua"}
